 CellLabel->"In[189]:=",
 CellID->139192339,ExpressionUUID->"6b72382d-b54f-604e-893f-698e03971b92"],

Cell["\<\
Intercept = 12.2828; In Poisson GLM, this is the log of expected death counts \
in Nigeria in base year, 2000. 
Intercept exponentiates to give 215,942 expected death count in baseline year.

Slope= -0.0517
Slope exponentiates to give multiplicative factor by which death change each \
year = 0.949<1 means deaths are falling by roughly 5% per year in Nigeria

p-value = 0.0; decline in Nigeria is statistically significant

Deviance table shows the amount of deviance explained by the year.

Akaike Information Criterion, AIC = 10,256 used for model comparison\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9860563457724857`*^9, 3.9860565756292877`*^9}, {
  3.9860566745961895`*^9, 3.986056715499428*^9}, {3.9860567963810673`*^9, 
